course: dictionary
lesson: 5422
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word lady is a good example. In «Ladies and gentlemen, welcome», lady is a polite way to speak to women. In «Lady Luck», the word is used like a name for chance or fortune.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Pat the lollipop lady says «Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!» on rainy days.» Here a lollipop lady is a woman who helps children cross the road safely, and the rainy days tell you she is out in the weather every day.
explain: Lady can also be part of a longer phrase, like «old lady», «dinner lady» or «the lady at the shop». Read the whole phrase, not just the one word. Ask yourself: what job, person or idea is being described?
explain: Grammar can change a word too. Lady becomes ladies in the plural, and the plural of a word ending in s adds only an apostrophe in the possessive. So «the ladies' toilets» is correct, while «the children's toys» shows the rule for plurals that do not end in s.
fact: Lady is a noun, and its plural is ladies.
fact: «Lady» can mean a polite word for a woman, as in «Ladies and gentlemen».
fact: «Lady» can mean a woman with good manners, or in the past a woman of high rank, as in «Lady Jane».
fact: «Lady Luck» means chance or fortune, spoken of as if she were a person.
fact: Plurals ending in s add only an apostrophe to show ownership, as in «the ladies' toilets».
exercise: «Pat the lollipop lady says «Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!»» What is a lollipop lady? | *A woman who helps children cross the road safely | A sweet shop worker | A lady who lives in a castle | A teacher who plays the piano
exercise: Which is correct for a toilet for women? | *the ladies' toilets | the ladys' toilets | the ladie's toilets | the lady's toilets
exercise: «Lady Luck» means | a rich queen | a nice person who helps others | *chance or fortune | a kind old lady
test: «Ladies and gentlemen, please take your seats.» What does lady mean here? | *A polite word for women | A bird that sings at dawn | A woman of high rank in a castle | A large cake
test: In the Moon Festival, families look at the moon for «the lady Cháng'é and her jade rabbit». Who is the lady Cháng'é? | *A woman from an old Chinese story linked with the moon | A kind dinner lady at school | The name of a shop in the town | A pet rabbit from a family home
exam: In «the lady at the shop», what does lady mean? | A chance or fortune | A polite word for a woman | *A polite word for a woman who serves customers | A rabbit with jade fur
